\b\fs28 Yale Assure Lock 2 (Wi-Fi Smart Module) \'96 Control4 Driver\b0\fs20\par
\par
\b Unofficial community driver.\b0  Not affiliated with or supported by Yale, ASSA ABLOY, August Home, or Control4. Version 100.\par
\par
\b How it works\b0\par
The Assure Lock 2 Wi-Fi Smart Module has no local LAN API. This driver controls the lock through the Yale Access (formerly August) cloud at https://api-production.august.com over HTTPS. Lock and unlock therefore depend on your internet connection and on that cloud service being reachable. Typical round trip is 1-4 seconds.\par
\par
The API is the private phone-app API, documented only by community reverse engineering (see the yalexs project). Yale may change or break it without notice.\par
\par
\b Setup\b0\par
1. Set \b Brand\b0  (Yale Access if you use the Yale Access app, August if your account was created in the August app), \b Login Method\b0 , \b Username\b0  and \b Password\b0 .\par
2. Run the action \b 1 - Sign In / Request Verification Code\b0 . Yale sends a 6-digit code to your email or phone.\par
3. Enter that code in the \b Verification Code\b0  property, then run \b 2 - Submit Verification Code\b0 .\par
4. Run \b 3 - Discover Locks\b0 . With a single lock on the account it is selected automatically; otherwise copy the Lock ID printed in the Lua output into the \b Lock ID\b0  property.\par
5. Polling starts automatically. You may blank out the Password afterwards - the driver keeps and refreshes an access token instead.\par
\par
\b What is supported\b0\par
\bullet  Lock, Unlock and Toggle, with lock state reported back to Navigator and to programming.\par
\bullet  Battery level, mapped to the proxy's normal / warning / critical states (warning at 40%, critical at 15%).\par
\bullet  DoorSense door position, exposed as a separate contact sensor binding. If your lock has no DoorSense magnet paired, this binding simply never reports.\par
\bullet  Event history (who locked or unlocked and when), from the account activity feed.\par
\bullet  Reading the keypad PIN code list.\par
\par
\b What is NOT supported\b0\par
\bullet  \b Creating, editing or deleting PIN codes.\b0  There is no confirmed API endpoint for these operations, so ADD_USER, EDIT_USER and DELETE_USER are deliberately inert: they log a message and change nothing. Manage codes in the Yale Access app. This is a safety decision - firing unverified write requests at a door lock's credential list is not worth the risk.\par
\bullet  Lock settings (auto-lock time, volume, language, lockout timers, admin code). No confirmed endpoints exist, so these capabilities are advertised as false and no Navigator settings screen is offered for them.\par
\par
\b Troubleshooting\b0\par
Set \b Log Mode\b0  to \ldblquote Print and Log\rdblquote  and watch the Lua tab. Every request and response code is logged; credentials and tokens are redacted. The \b - Print Debug Info\b0  action dumps the full driver state. If the Auth State property shows a rejected token, re-run action 1.
